{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "c269458e-113e-88c4-99dc-c29b845e5175",
  "created_at": "2026-01-12T13:36:28-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Min-jun Kim",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:28:26-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:28:32-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes. Good afternoon. I'm calling about a manhole cover. And a puddle. Well, the puddle first, I guess."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:28:42-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, sure. Where's the puddle, is it out on the street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:28:48-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's my driveway. The apron, the part at the bottom where it meets the street. It holds a puddle, and the water runs down toward the garage door instead of out to the street. That is the wrong direction."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:29:07-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ugh, yeah, that's not what you want. Is this since the storm over the weekend?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:29:15-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Since the storm, yes. The coastal one, Friday and Saturday. Two days ago now. The puddle was there after, and it's still half there today. It never used to sit like that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:29:31-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And has any water actually gotten into the garage?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:29:37-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A little at the door, the bottom edge. I put a towel down. It's annoying, that's all. I don't want it to turn into something worse."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:29:50-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understandable. You mentioned a manhole cover too?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:29:54-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Out in the street, a few feet from the apron. The cover looks off. Maybe an inch. One side sits higher than the other, like it got bumped or the ground moved."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:30:11-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "An inch, okay. Is it rocking or making noise when cars go over it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:30:19-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I heard a clunk once, when a truck went by. So maybe. I didn't stand there and watch it, I was in the kitchen."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:30:31-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] That's good to know. Is it a round cover in the middle of the road, or off to the side near the curb?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:30:43-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Closer to the curb. Not the middle. Round, yes, iron I think. Not the little grate for the rain, a real cover."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:30:54-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so that sounds like a sewer or utility structure, not just the catch basin. I can take the report for it. What I need is the address or the nearest cross street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:31:11-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hm. I'd rather not give the address on this call, honestly. I just want to know who to call to get it checked. Is that you, or somebody else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:31:26-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it's us for the street and the covers, mostly. But I can't send a crew to a spot I can't find. If you'd rather not say it now, you could call back when you have a minute and give a location to whoever picks up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:31:49-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. So this department. Public Works. That is the right door."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:31:56-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right door, yes. Street drainage, the covers, the apron where it meets the road. If the manhole turns out to belong to a utility company, we'd pass it along to them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:32:12-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A utility company. Which one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:32:15-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Depends what's underneath. Could be sewer, could be a phone or electric vault. Whoever goes out can tell by the markings on the lid."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:32:27-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. That makes sense. Markings. I didn't look at the lid, only the edge."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:32:35-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No need to go out in traffic. If you can, just don't park over it and keep kids and bikes away from that spot until someone looks."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:32:49-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No kids. Just me and the car. I can park somewhere else."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:32:56-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. And for the driveway puddle, is the apron cracked, or is it more that it's settled and dips?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:33:06-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It dips. A low spot. The storm made it obvious. Before, I never noticed, a little damp maybe."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:33:15-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. The apron part in the public right of way is something an inspector can look at. The part on your property would be yours to fix, so it helps to have them tell you where the line is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:33:34-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hm. Yes. That is fair. I just want someone to say what it is. Because right now I'm guessing, and guessing costs money."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:33:46-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. So here's what I'd do. Call back this afternoon or tomorrow morning, ask for the line to log a street inspection, and have the address and the closest cross street ready."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:34:02-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tomorrow is fine. Today I'm running around. Honestly, I was in the middle of errands when I noticed the lid, and then I got a surprise at the grocery. My favorite store, they're rearranging all the aisles. Everything moves. Eleven years I knew where the rice was."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:34:25-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that's the worst. You finally learn the place and they shuffle it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:34:32-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Now I have to hunt. Anyway. That is not your department."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:34:39-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, ha, not mine. Can I at least get a callback number so there's a note on this?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:34:48-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. It's four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-eight-eight."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:34:51-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-eight-eight. And the name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:34:55-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Min-jun Kim. M-I-N, dash, J-U-N. Kim, like it sounds."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:35:00-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, Mr. Kim. I'll put a note that you called about a manhole cover sitting about an inch off near the curb and a low spot on the driveway apron after the weekend storm, and that you'll call back with the location."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:35:21-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. That's it. And the water going toward the garage. Please put that. The garage door."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:35:30-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Toward the garage door, got it. That's the part that makes it a priority for them to look at."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:35:40-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. How long, usually? After a storm. Days? Weeks?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:35:45-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "After a big one, crews are busy with the worst spots first, so it could be a few days. A cover that's shifted tends to get looked at sooner than a puddle, though."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:36:02-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. A few days. I can live with a few days. A few weeks, no."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:36:10-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Call back with that location and we'll get it moving."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:36:16-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I will. Thank you, Denise. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:36:21-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too, Mr. Kim. Good luck finding your rice."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T13:36:26-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ha. Thanks. Bye."
    }
  ],
